  "name": "duplicate-number-value-equal",
  "purpose": "Lifecycle value equality compares JSON numbers as exact mathematical values, so the spelling a number arrived in is not content. Two deliveries at the same identity whose only difference is an integer written 1 against the same integer written 1.0 carry the same value, and the second is an exact retransmission: it is suppressed wholesale, changes nothing, and is counted. A reducer comparing lexemes would call this a conflicting duplicate and fail a stream that repeated itself faithfully.",
